translated_text:
REGENT OF OGAN KOMERING ULU SELATAN

REGENT OF OGAN KOMERING ULU SELATAN

SOUTH SUMATRA PROVINCE

REGIONAL REGULATION OF OGAN KOMERING ULU SELATAN REGENCY NUMBER 7 OF 2020

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

THE REGENT OF OGAN KOMERING ULU SELATAN,

Considering : a. that the government has the obligation to provide protection, advancement, enforcement and fulfillment of Human Rights for every citizen including the Rights

of Women and Children;

b. that Women and Children are vulnerable groups who tend to experience violence and discrimination and therefore need to receive optimal protection;

c. that the fulfillment of the constitutional rights of Women and Children as well as the improvement of the quality of life of Women and Children, is one of the mandatory affairs that is the duty, authority and responsibility of

the Regency Government;

d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Protection of

Women and Children;

In view of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of

the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);

3. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235), as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 17 of 2016 concerning the Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 of 2016 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2016 Number 237, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5946);

4. Law Number 37 of 2003 concerning the Establishment of East Ogan Komering Ulu Regency, South Ogan Komering Ulu Regency and Ogan Ilir Regency in South Sumatra Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 152, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4347);

5. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);

6. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Crime of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);

7. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587), as has been amended several times, most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);

8. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation of Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);

9. Government Regulation Number 59 of 2019 concerning the Implementation of Coordination of Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2019

Number 160, Supplement to the State Gazette of the

Republic of Indonesia Number 6382);

10. Regulation of the Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards in the Field of Integrated Services for Women and

Children Victims of Violence (State News of the Republic

of Indonesia of 2010 Number 483);

11. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 15 of 2010 concerning General Guidelines for Handling Children in

Conflict with the Law (State News of the Republic of

Indonesia of 2010 Number 483);

12. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 19 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for the Empowerment of Women Victims of

Violence (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011

Number

With the Mutual Approval of

THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES

OF OGAN KOMERING ULU SELATAN REGENCY

and

THE REGENT OF OGAN KOMERING ULU SELATAN

HAS DECIDED:

To establish : A REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING THE PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN.

text:
Pasal 2

(1) Penyelenggaraan Perlindungan Perempuan berdasarkan asas :

a. kepentingan terbaik bagi Perempuan;
b. keadilan gender dan kesetaraan gender;
c. kearifan lokal; dan
d. kepastian hukum.
(2) Penyelenggaraan Perlindungan Anak berdasarkan asas: a. non diskriminasi;
b. kepentingan yang terbaik bagi Anak;
c. hak untuk hidup, kelangsungan hidup, dan perkembangan;
d. penghargaan terhadap pendapat Anak; dan e. kepastian hukum.

translated_text:
Article 2

(1) The implementation of Protection of Women is based on the principles of:

a. the best interests of Women;
b. gender justice and gender equality;
c. local wisdom; and
d. legal certainty.
(2) The implementation of Protection of Children is based on the principles of: a. non-discrimination;
b. the best interests of the Child;
c. the right to life, survival, and development;
d. respect for the views of the Child; and e. legal certainty.

text:
Pasal 3

Pengaturan Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak bertujuan: a. sebagai pedoman bagi Pemerintah Kabupaten dalam perencanaan, kebijakan dan strategi Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak;

b. melindungi Perempuan dan Anak dari tindakan, keputusan dan kebijakan yang melanggar hak Perempuan dan Anak;

c. mencegah terjadinya pelanggaran Hak Perempuan dan Anak;

d. meningkatkan pemberdayaan terhadap Perempuan dan Anak;

e. meningkatkan peran dan nilai kearifan lokal dalam Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak; dan

f. meningkatkan peran Perangkat Daerah dan non

Pemerintah di Kabupaten dalam upaya Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak.

translated_text:
Article 3

The regulation of Protection of Women and Children aims to: a. serve as a guideline for the Regency Government in planning, policies and strategies for the Protection of Women and Children;

b. protect Women and Children from actions, decisions and policies that violate the rights of Women and Children;

c. prevent the occurrence of violations of the Rights of Women and Children;

d. enhance the empowerment of Women and Children;

e. enhance the role and values of local wisdom in the Protection of Women and Children; and

f. enhance the role of Regional Apparatus and non-

Government entities in the Regency in efforts for the Protection of Women and Children.

text:
Pasal 4

Ruang lingkup pengaturan Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak meliputi:

a. pencegahan;
b. penyelenggaraan Perlindungan Hak Perempuan dan Anak;
c. penanganan;
d. pemberdayaan; dan
e. pembinaan dan pengawasan.

translated_text:
Article 4

The scope of regulation of the Protection of Women and Children includes:

a. prevention;
b. implementation of Protection of the Rights of Women and Children;
c. handling;
d. empowerment; and
e. guidance and supervision.

text:
Pasal 5

Setiap Perempuan berhak:

a. memperoleh perlindungan dari tindakan diskriminasi; b. memperoleh perlindungan dari eksploitasi ekonomi dan eksploitasi seksual;
c. memperoleh perlindungan dari kekerasan fisik, psikologis, seksual, dan penelantaran;
d. memperoleh pekerjaan yang layak sesuai kemampuannya;
e. memperoleh cuti kerja dengan menerima upah/ gaji sesuai dengan peraturan perundang-undangan; f. memperoleh pendidikan dan pengajaran di semua jenis, jenjang dan jalur pendidikan;
g. mendapatkan perlindungan khusus dalam pelaksanaan pekerjaan atau profesinya terhadap hal-hal yang dapat mengancam keselamatan dan/atau kesehatannya berkenaan dengan fungsi reproduksi Perempuan;
h. berhak untuk memilih, dipilih, diangkat dalam pekerjaan, jabatan, dan profesi sesuai dengan persyaratan dan peraturan perundang-undangan; dan
i. pemilikan dan pengelolaan harta bersama dalam perkawinan sesuai dengan ketentuan Peraturan Perundang-undangan.

translated_text:
Article 5

Every Woman has the right to:

a. obtain protection from acts of discrimination; b. obtain protection from economic exploitation and sexual exploitation;
c. obtain protection from physical, psychological, sexual violence, and neglect;
d. obtain decent work in accordance with her capabilities;
e. obtain work leave while receiving wages/salary in accordance with laws and regulations; f. obtain education and instruction in all types, levels and pathways of education;
g. obtain special protection in the performance of work or profession against matters that may threaten her safety and/or health in connection with the reproductive function of Women;
h. have the right to choose, be chosen, be appointed in employment, positions, and professions in accordance with requirements and laws and regulations; and
i. ownership and management of joint property in marriage in accordance with the provisions of Laws and Regulations.

text:
Pasal 6

(1) Setiap Anak berhak :

a. setiap anak berhak atas perlindungan oleh orang tua, keluarga, masyarakat, dan negara;
b. hak anak adalah hak asasi manusia dan untuk kepentingannya hak anak itu diakui dan dilindungi oleh hukum bahkan sejak dalam kandungan;
c. setiap anak sejak dalam kandungan, berhak untuk hidup, mempertahankan hidup, dan meningkatkan taraf kehidupannya;
d. setiap anak sejak kelahirannya, berhak atas suatu nama dan status kewarganegaraan;
e. setiap anak yang cacat fisik dan atau mental berhak memperoleh perawatan, pendidikan, pelatihan, dan bantuan khusus atas biaya negara, untuk menjamin kehidupannya sesuai dengan martabat kemanusiaan, meningkatkan rasa percaya diri, dan kemampuan berpartisipasi dalam kehidupan masyarakat, berbangsa, dan bernegara;
f. setiap anak berhak untuk beribadah menurut agamanya, berfikir, berekspresi sesuai dengan tingkat intelektualitas dan usianya di bawah bimbingan orang tua dan/atau wali;
g. setiap anak berhak untuk mengetahui siapa orang tuanya, dibesarkan, dan diasuh oleh orang tuanya sendiri;
h. dalam hal orang tua anak tidak mampu membesarkan dan memelihara anaknya dengan baik, maka anak tersebut boleh diasuh atau diangkat sebagai anak oleh orang lain sesuai dengan ketentuan peraturan perundang-undangan;
i. setiap anak berhak untuk dibesarkan, dipelihara, dirawat, dididik, diarahkan, dan dibimbing kehidupannya oleh orang tua atau walinya sampai dewasa sesuai dengan ketentuan peraturan perundang-undangan;
j. setiap anak berhak untuk mendapatkan orang tua angkat atau wali berdasarkan putusan pengadilan apabila kedua orang tua telah meninggal dunia atau karena suatu sebab yang sah tidak dapat menjalankan kewajibannya sebagai orang tua;
k. orang tua angkat atau wali sebagaimana dimaksud dalam huruf j harus menjalankan kewajiban sebagai orang tua yang sesungguhnya;
l. setiap anak berhak untuk mendapatkan perlindungan hukum dari segala bentuk kekerasan fisik atau mental, penelantaran, perlakuan buruk, dan pelecehan seksual selama dalam pengasuhan orang tua atau walinya, atau pihak lain maupun yang bertanggung jawab atas pengasuhan anak tersebut;
m. dalam hal orang tua, wali, atau pengasuh anak melakukan segala bentuk penganiayaan fisik atau mental, penelantaran, perlakuan bentuk, dan pelecehan seksual termasuk pemerkosaan, dan atau pembunuhan terhadap anak yang seharusnya dilindungi, maka harus dikenakan pemberatan hukuman;
n. setiap anak berhak untuk tidak dipisahkan dari orang tuanya secara bertentangan dengan kehendak anak sendiri, kecuali jika ada alasan dan aturan hukum yang sah yang menunjukkan bahwa pemisahan itu demi kepentingan terbaik bagi anak;
o. dalam keadaan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam huruf n, hak anak untuk tetap bertemu langsung dan berhubungan pribadi secara tetap dengan orang tuanya tetap dijamin oleh Undang-undang;
p. setiap anak berhak untuk memperoleh pendidikan dan pengajaran dalam rangka pengembangan pribadinya sesuai dengan minat, bakat, dan tingkat kecerdasannya;
q. setiap anak berhak mencari, menerima, dan memberikan informasi sesuai dengan tingkat intelektualitas dan usianya demi pengembangan dirinya sepanjang sesuai dengan nilai-nilai kesusilaan dan kepatutan;
r. setiap anak berhak untuk beristirahat, bergaul dengan anak yang sebaya, bermain, berekreasi, dan berkreasi sesuai dengan minat, bakat, dan tingkat kecerdasannya demi pengembangan dirinya;
s. setiap anak berhak untuk memperoleh pelayanan kesehatan dan jaminan sosial secara layak, sesuai dengan kebutuhan fisik dan mental spiritualnya;
t. setiap anak berhak untuk tidak dilibatkan di dalam peristiwa peperangan, sengketa bersenjata, kerusuhan sosial, dan peristiwa lain yang mengandung unsur kekerasan;
u. setiap anak berhak untuk memperoleh perlindungan dari kegiatan eksploitasi ekonomi dan setiap pekerjaan yang membahayakan dirinya, sehingga dapat mengganggu pendidikan, kesehatan fisik, moral, kehidupan sosial, dan mental spiritualnya;
v. setiap anak berhak untuk memperoleh perlindungan dari kegiatan eksploitasi dan pelecehan seksual, penculikan, perdagangan anak, serta dari berbagai bentuk penyalahgunaan narkotika, psikotropika, dan zat adiktif lainnya;
w. setiap anak berhak untuk tidak dijadikan sasaran penganiayaan, penyiksaan, atau penjatuhan hukuman yang tidak manusiawi;
x. setiap anak berhak untuk tidak dirampas kebebasannya secara melawan hukum;
y. penangkapan, penahanan, atau pidana penjara anak hanya boleh dilakukan sesuai dengan hukum yang berlaku dan hanya dapat dilaksanakan sebagai upaya terakhir;
z. setiap anak yang dirampas kebebasannya berhak mendapatkan perlakuan secara manusiawi dan dengan memperhatikan kebutuhan pengembangan pribadi sesuai dengan usianya dan harus dipisahkan dari orang dewasa, kecuali demi kepentingannya; aa. setiap anak yang dirampas kebebasannya berhak memperoleh bantuan hukum atau bantuan lainnya secara efektif dalam setiap tahapan upaya hukum yang berlaku; bb. setiap anak yang dirampas kebebasannya berhak untuk membela diri dan memperoleh keadilan di depan Pengadilan Anak yang obyektif dan tidak memihak dalam sidang yang tertutup untuk umum.
(2) Setiap anak yang menjadi korban atau pelaku kekerasan seksual atau yang berhadapan dengan hukum berhak dirahasiakan.
(3) Setiap Anak Penyandang Disabilitas selain mendapatkan hak sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) juga berhak memperoleh:
a. pendidikan luar biasa/pendidikan khusus; b. rehabilitasi;
c. bantuan sosial; dan
d. pemeliharaan taraf kesejahteraan sosial.
(4) Setiap Anak yang memiliki keunggulan berhak mendapatkan pendidikan khusus.

translated_text:
Article 6

(1) Every Child has the right:

a. every child has the right to protection by parents, family, community, and the state;
b. the rights of the child are human rights and for their benefit the rights of the child are recognized and protected by law even from the womb;
c. every child from the womb has the right to live, survive, and improve their standard of living;
d. every child from birth has the right to a name and citizenship status;
e. every child with physical and/or mental disabilities has the right to receive care, education, training, and special assistance at state expense, to ensure their life in accordance with human dignity, increase self-confidence, and the ability to participate in community, national, and state life;
f. every child has the right to worship according to their religion, think, and express themselves in accordance with their intellectual level and age under the guidance of parents and/or guardians;
g. every child has the right to know who their parents are, to be raised, and cared for by their own parents;
h. in the event that the child's parents are unable to raise and care for the child properly, then the child may be cared for or adopted as a child by another person in accordance with the provisions of legislation;
i. every child has the right to be raised, cared for, nurtured, educated, directed, and guided in their life by their parents or guardians until adulthood in accordance with the provisions of legislation;
j. every child has the right to obtain adoptive parents or a guardian based on a court decision if both parents have died or due to a valid reason are unable to carry out their obligations as parents;
k. adoptive parents or guardians as referred to in letter j must carry out the obligations of actual parents;
l. every child has the right to receive legal protection from all forms of physical or mental violence, neglect, maltreatment, and sexual abuse while in the care of parents or guardians, or other parties responsible for the care of the child;
m. in the event that parents, guardians, or caregivers of the child commit any form of physical or mental abuse, neglect, maltreatment, and sexual abuse including rape, and/or murder of the child who should be protected, they must be subject to aggravated punishment;
n. every child has the right not to be separated from their parents against the child's own wishes, unless there are legal reasons and regulations that show that the separation is in the best interests of the child;
o. in the circumstances as referred to in letter n, the child's right to continue to meet directly and maintain personal contact regularly with their parents is still guaranteed by law;
p. every child has the right to obtain education and teaching in the context of personal development in accordance with their interests, talents, and level of intelligence;
q. every child has the right to seek, receive, and provide information in accordance with their intellectual level and age for their self-development as long as it is in accordance with moral values and propriety;
r. every child has the right to rest, associate with children of the same age, play, recreate, and create in accordance with their interests, talents, and level of intelligence for their self-development;
s. every child has the right to obtain health services and social security appropriately, in accordance with their physical and spiritual mental needs;
t. every child has the right not to be involved in war events, armed conflicts, social unrest, and other events containing elements of violence;
u. every child has the right to obtain protection from economic exploitation activities and any work that endangers them, so that it can disrupt their education, physical health, morals, social life, and spiritual mentality;
v. every child has the right to obtain protection from exploitation and sexual abuse, kidnapping, child trafficking, as well as from various forms of narcotics, psychotropics, and other addictive substances abuse;
w. every child has the right not to be subjected to persecution, torture, or imposition of inhuman punishment;
x. every child has the right not to be deprived of their freedom unlawfully;
y. arrest, detention, or imprisonment of a child may only be carried out in accordance with applicable law and can only be implemented as a last resort;
z. every child deprived of their freedom has the right to receive humane treatment and with attention to the needs of personal development according to their age and must be separated from adults, except in their best interests; aa. every child deprived of their freedom has the right to obtain legal assistance or other assistance effectively at every stage of applicable legal proceedings; bb. every child deprived of their freedom has the right to defend themselves and obtain justice before an objective and impartial Juvenile Court in a hearing closed to the public.
(2) Every child who is a victim or perpetrator of sexual violence or who is in conflict with the law has the right to confidentiality.
(3) Every Child with Disabilities in addition to receiving the rights as referred to in paragraph (1) is also entitled to obtain:
a. special education/special education; b. rehabilitation;
c. social assistance; and
d. maintenance of social welfare standards.
(4) Every Child who has excellence has the right to receive special education.

text:
Pasal 8

(1) Pemerintah Kabupaten dalam upaya perlindungan terhadap Anak wajib dan bertanggung jawab: a. menghormati pemenuhan hak Anak tanpa membedakan suku, agama, ras, golongan, jenis kelamin, etnik, budaya dan bahasa, status hukum, urutan kelahiran, dan kondisi fisik dan/atau mental; b. memberikan dukungan sarana, prasarana, dan ketersediaan sumber daya manusia dalam penyelenggaraan Perlindungan Anak;

c. menjamin perlindungan, pemeliharaan, dan kesejahteraan Anak dengan memperhatikan hak dan kewajiban Orang Tua, Wali, atau orang lain yang secara hukum bertanggung jawab terhadap Anak;

d. menjamin Anak untuk menyampaikan haknya menyampaikan pendapat sesuai dengan usia dan tingkat kecerdasan Anak;

e. menetapkan dan melaksanakan kebijakan serta program/kegiatan perlindungan terhadap hak Anak; f. melakukan kerjasama dengan masyarakat dan/atau Organisasi Kemasyarakatan dalam penyelenggaraan perlindungan Anak sesuai dengan ketentuan Peraturan Perundang-undangan;

g. melakukan rehabilitasi terhadap Anak yang menjadi korban tindak kekerasan;

h. memberikan perlindungan khusus kepada Anak: 1. dalam situasi darurat;

2. yang berhadapan dengan hukum;

3. dari kelompok minoritas dan terisolasi;

4. yang dieksploitasi secara ekonomi dan/atau seksual;

5. yang menjadi korban penyalahgunaan narkotika, alkohol, psikotropika, dan zat adiktif lainnya; 6. yang menjadi korban pornografi;

7. dengan HIV/AIDS;

8. korban penculikan, penjualan, dan/atau perdagangan;

9. korban kekerasan fisik dan/atau psikis;

10. korban kejahatan seksual;

11. korban jaringan terorisme;

12. penyandang disabilitas;

13. korban perlakuan salah dan penelantaran; 14. dengan perilaku sosial menyimpang; dan

15. yang menjadi korban stigmatisasi dari pelabelan terkait dengan kondisi orang tuanya.

i. menyelenggarakan pendidikan inklusif bagi Anak yang berkebutuhan khusus;

j. melakukan tindakan preventif dalam rangka mencegah terjadinya pelanggaran terhadap Anak; dan

k. melaksanakan dan mendukung kebijakan Nasional dalam penyelenggaraan Perlindungan Anak di Kabupaten yang dilakukan melalui upaya mewujudkan Kabupaten Layak Anak, Kecamatan Layak Anak dan Desa Layak Anak.

(2) Tanggung jawab Pemerintah Kabupaten dalam upaya perlindungan Anak sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan oleh DPPKBP-PPPA.

translated_text:
Article 8

(1) The Regency Government in its efforts to protect Children is obliged and responsible to: a. respect the fulfillment of Children's rights without distinguishing ethnicity, religion, race, class, gender, ethnic group, culture and language, legal status, birth order, and physical and/or mental condition; b. provide support for facilities, infrastructure, and availability of human resources in the administration of Child Protection;

c. guarantee the protection, maintenance, and welfare of Children with due regard to the rights and obligations of Parents, Guardians, or other persons legally responsible for Children;

d. guarantee Children to express their right to express opinions in accordance with the age and intelligence level of Children;

e. establish and implement policies and programs/activities for the protection of Children's rights; f. cooperate with the community and/or Community Organizations in administering Child Protection in accordance with the provisions of Laws and Regulations;

g. conduct rehabilitation for Children who are victims of acts of violence;

h. provide special protection to Children: 1. in emergency situations;

2. in conflict with the law;

3. from minority and isolated groups;

4. who are exploited economically and/or sexually;

5. who are victims of narcotics, alcohol, psychotropic, and other addictive substance abuse; 6. who are victims of pornography;

7. with HIV/AIDS;

8. victims of abduction, sale, and/or trafficking;

9. victims of physical and/or psychological violence;

10. victims of sexual crimes;

11. victims of terrorist networks;

12. persons with disabilities;

13. victims of mistreatment and neglect; 14. with deviant social behavior; and

15. who are victims of stigmatization from labeling related to their parents' condition.

i. organize inclusive education for Children with special needs;

j. take preventive measures to prevent violations against Children; and

k. implement and support National policies in the administration of Child Protection in the Regency conducted through efforts to realize Child-Friendly Regency, Child-Friendly District and Child-Friendly Village.

(2) The responsibility of the Regency Government in efforts to protect Children as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented by DPPKBP-PPPA.

text:
Paragraf 1

Tanggung Jawab Terhadap Perlindungan Hak Perempuan Pasal 11 Tanggung jawab keluarga dalam upaya perlindungan perempuan meliputi:

a. melindungi perempuan dari konflik dan kekerasan dalam rumah tangga yang merendahkan martabat perempuan;
b. memberikan kesempatan yang sama pada perempuan untuk mengembangkan diri di bidang:
1. pendidikan;
2. sosial;
3. ekonomi; dan
4. politik dan budaya.
c. mencegah terjadinya pelanggaran terhadap hak perempuan dalam rumah tangga.

translated_text:
Paragraph 1

Responsibility for the Protection of Women's Rights Article 11 Family responsibilities in efforts to protect women include:

a. protecting women from conflict and domestic violence that degrades the dignity of women;
b. providing equal opportunities for women to develop themselves in the fields of:
1. education;
2. social;
3. economy; and
4. politics and culture.
c. preventing violations of women's rights in the household.

text:
Paragraf 2

Tanggung Jawab Terhadap Perlindungan Hak Anak Pasal 12

(1) Orang tua dalam upaya perlindungan terhadap Anak bertanggungjawab:

a. mengasuh, memelihara, mendidik, dan melindungi Anak;
b. menumbuh kembangkan Anak sesuai dengan kemampuan, bakat, dan minatnya;
c. memberikan pendidikan formal dan non formal; d. membimbing Anak berperilaku sesuai dengan agama, etika dan moral serta adat istiadat; dan e. mencegah teIjadinya perkawinan pada usia Anak. (2) Dalam hal orang tua tidak ada, atau tidak diketahui keberadaannya, atau karena suatu sebab, tidak dapat melaksanakan kewajiban dan tanggung jawabnya, maka kewajiban dan tanggung jawab sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dapat beralih pada keluarga.

translated_text:
Paragraph 2

Responsibility for the Protection of Children's Rights Article 12

(1) Parents in efforts to protect Children are responsible for:

a. raising, maintaining, educating, and protecting Children;
b. developing Children in accordance with their abilities, talents, and interests;
c. providing formal and non-formal education; d. guiding Children to behave in accordance with religion, ethics and morals as well as customs; and e. preventing marriage at Child age. (2) In the event that parents do not exist, or their whereabouts are unknown, or for some reason, are unable to carry out their obligations and responsibilities, then the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1) may be transferred to the family.

text:
Pasal 13

(1) Upaya yang dilakukan Pemerintah Kabupaten dalam rangka mencegah terjadinya pelanggaran terhadap hak Perempuan meliputi:

a. penyelenggaraan sosialisasi mengenai pencegahan kekerasan terhadap Perempuan dengan mengoptimalkan peran lembaga adat, budaya, agama dan organisasi kemasyarakatan;
b. penyediaan pedoman tentang penanganan tindak kekerasan terhadap Perempuan;
c. melibatkan peran serta masyarakat dalam pemulihan dan reintegrasi;
d. pengembangan database dan sistem informasi yang terintegrasi tentang tindak kekerasan terhadap Perempuan;
e. pengembangan program pemberdayaan keluarga; f. penguatan fungsi organisasi kemasyarakatan yang bergerak di bidang pemberdayaan Perempuan; dan g. penyediaan fasilitas umum yang nyaman dan aman untuk Perempuan.
(2) Upaya yang dilakukan Pemerintah Kabupaten dalam rangka mencegah terjadinya pelanggaran hak Anak meliputi:
a. pencegahan tindak kekerasan terhadap Anak dengan mengoptimalkan peran lembaga adat, budaya, agama dan organisasi kemasyarakatan; b. pengembangan sekolah ramah Anak;
c. mendorong peningkatan partisipasi anak melalui pembentukan Forum Anak;
d. penyediaan pedoman tentang penanganan tindak kekerasan terhadap Anak;
e. melibatkan peran serta masyarakat dalam layanan pemulihan dan reintegrasi Anak korban kekerasan; f. pengembangan database dan sistem informasi yang terintegrasi tentang tindak kekerasan terhadap Anak;
g. penguatan fungsi organisasi kemasyarakatan yang bergerak di bidang perlindungan Anak; dan
h. mendorong pembentukan Kabupaten Layak Anak.

translated_text:
Article 13

(1) Efforts made by the Regency Government to prevent violations of Women's rights include:

a. conducting socialization on the prevention of violence against Women by optimizing the role of customary, cultural, religious institutions and community organizations;
b. providing guidelines on handling acts of violence against Women;
c. involving community participation in recovery and reintegration;
d. developing an integrated database and information system on acts of violence against Women;
e. developing family empowerment programs; f. strengthening the function of community organizations working in the field of Women's empowerment; and g. providing comfortable and safe public facilities for Women.
(2) Efforts made by the Regency Government to prevent violations of Children's rights include:
a. preventing acts of violence against Children by optimizing the role of customary, cultural, religious institutions and community organizations; b. developing child-friendly schools;
c. encouraging increased child participation through the establishment of Child Forums;
d. providing guidelines on handling acts of violence against Children;
e. involving community participation in recovery services and reintegration of child victims of violence; f. developing an integrated database and information system on acts of violence against Children;
g. strengthening the function of community organizations working in the field of Child protection; and
h. encouraging the establishment of Child-Friendly Regency.

text:
Pasal 15

(1) Upaya yang dilakukan pihak keluarga dalam rangka mencegah terjadinya pelanggaran terhadap hak Perempuan meliputi:

a. perlindungan perempuan dari berbagai pelanggaran hak dalam rumah tangga; dan
b. mendorong terbentuknya keluarga yang harmonis, edukatif dan demokratis;
(2) Upaya yang dilakukan pihak orang tua dalam rangka mencegah terjadinya pelanggaran terhadap hak Anak meliputi:
a. pemberian tauladan yang baik kepada anak sesuai ajaran agama dan adat;
b. pengawasan anak dalam beraktivitas di dalam ataupun di luar rumah;
c. pemberian peluang bagi anak berdialog menyampaikan pendapat secara demokratis; dan d. perlindungan anak dari berbagai tindak pelanggaran hak Anak dalam rumah tangga.

translated_text:
Article 15

(1) Efforts made by the family to prevent violations of Women's rights include:

a. protecting women from various violations of rights in the household; and
b. encouraging the formation of harmonious, educative and democratic families;
(2) Efforts made by parents to prevent violations of Children's rights include:
a. providing good examples to children in accordance with religious teachings and customs;
b. supervising children in activities inside or outside the home;
c. providing opportunities for children to engage in dialogue to express opinions democratically; and d. protecting children from various acts of violation of Children's rights in the household.

text:
Pasal 16

Pemerintah Kabupaten menyelenggarakan Perlindungan Perempuan dengan melibatkan:

a. keluarga;
b. tokoh masyarakat;
c. pemuka agama;
d. guru dan/atau akademisi;
e. masyarakat; dan
f. organisasi kemasyarakatan di bidang perlindungan Perempuan.

translated_text:
Article 16

The Regency Government organizes the Protection of Women by involving:

a. family;
b. community leaders;
c. religious leaders;
d. teachers and/or academics;
e. society; and
f. community organizations in the field of Women's protection.

text:
Pasal 23

(1) Upaya Pemerintah Kabupaten memberikan perlindungan Anak di bidang kesehatan meliputi: a. pelayanan kesehatan bebas biaya bagi Anak dari keluarga miskin;

b. penyelenggaraan kesehatan yang optimal bagi Anak agar memperoleh derajat kesehatan yang baik sejak dalam kandungan;

c. penjaminan agar bayi menerima ASI eksklusif dari ibunya secara benar dan wajar;

d. menjamin Anak mendapat gizi yang cukup; e. menjamin Anak yang baru lahir dilakukan screening; dan

f. menjamin penyediaan pemantauan pertumbuhan dan perkembangan balita dan anak usia pra sekolah.

(2) Pemerintah Kabupaten, keluarga, dan orang tua melindungi anak dari upaya transplantasi organ tubuhnya untuk pihak lain.

translated_text:
Article 23

(1) The Regency Government's efforts to provide Child protection in the health sector include: a. free health services for Children from poor families;

b. organizing optimal health for Children to obtain a good degree of health from the womb;

c. ensuring that babies receive exclusive breastfeeding from their mothers properly and naturally;

d. ensuring Children receive adequate nutrition; e. ensuring that newborn Children are screened; and

f. ensuring the provision of monitoring the growth and development of toddlers and pre-school age children.

(2) The Regency Government, family, and parents protect children from attempts to transplant their body organs to other parties.

text:
Pasal 32

(1) Ketentuan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 31 dapat dikecualikan bagi Anak yang berumur antara 13 (tiga belas) tahun sampai dengan 15 (lima belas) tahun, untuk melakukan pekerjaan ringan sepanjang tidak mengganggu perkembangan dan kesehatan fisik, mental, dan sosial.

(2) Pengusaha yang mempekerjakan Anak pada pekerjaan ringan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) harus memenuhi persyaratan meliputi:

a. izin tertulis dari orang tua atau wali;
b. perjanjian kerja antara pengusaha dengan orang tua atau wali;
c. waktu kerja maksimum 3 (tiga) jam;
d. dilakukan pada siang hari dan tidak mengganggu waktu sekolah;
e. keselamatan dan kesehatan kerja;
f. adanya hubungan kerja yang jeIas; dan
g. menerima upah sesuai dengan ketentuan peraturan perundang-undangan.
(3) Ketentuan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) huruf a, huruf b, huruf f, dan huruf g dikecualikan bagi Anak yang bekerja pada usaha keluarganya.

translated_text:
Article 32

(1) The provisions as referred to in Article 31 may be exempted for Children aged between 13 (thirteen) years to 15 (fifteen) years, to perform light work as long as it does not interfere with physical, mental, and social development and health.

(2) Employers who employ Children in light work as referred to in paragraph (1) must meet the requirements including:

a. written permission from parents or guardians;
b. work agreement between the employer and the parents or guardians;
c. maximum working time of 3 (three) hours;
d. carried out during the day and does not interfere with school time;
e. occupational safety and health;
f. clear employment relationship; and
g. receive wages in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
(3) The provisions as referred to in paragraph (2) letters a, b, f, and g are exempted for Children who work in their family business.

text:
Pasal 35

(1) Setiap orang dilarang mempekerjakan dan melibatkan Anak pada pekerjaan yang terburuk.

(2) Pekerjaan yang terburuk sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi:

a. segala pekerjaan dalam bentuk perbudakan atau sejenisnya;
b. segala pekerjaan yang memanfaatkan, menyediakan, atau menawarkan Anak untuk: 1. pelacuran;
2. produksi pornografi;
3. porno aksi;
4. perjudian;
5. produksi dan perdagangan minuman keras; 6. narkotika;
7. psikotropika; dan
8. zat adiktif Iainnya; dan/atau
c. semua pekerjaan yang membahayakan kesehatan, keselamatan, atau moral Anak.

translated_text:
Article 35

(1) Every person is prohibited from employing and involving Children in the worst forms of work.

(2) The worst forms of work as referred to in paragraph (1) include:

a. all work in the form of slavery or similar practices;
b. all work that exploits, provides, or offers Children for: 1. prostitution;
2. production of pornography;
3. pornographic performances;
4. gambling;
5. production and trade of alcoholic beverages; 6. narcotics;
7. psychotropics; and
8. other addictive substances; and/or
c. all work that endangers the health, safety, or morals of Children.

text:
Pasal 41

(1) Pelaksanaan penanganan Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 40 dilaksanakan melalui pelayanan terpadu.

(2) Pelayanan terpadu bagi Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) menggunakan prinsip:

a. responsif gender;
b. non diskriminasi;
c. hubungan setara dan menghormati;
d. menjaga kerahasiaan;
e. memberi rasa aman dan nyaman;
f. menghargai perbedaan individu;
g. tidak menghakimi;
h. menghormati pilihan dan keputusan korban; i. peka terhadap latar belakang dan kondisi korban dan pemakaian bahasa yang sesuai dan dimengerti oleh korban;
j. cepat dan sederhana;
k. empati;
l. pemenuhan hak Perempuan dan Anak; dan m. tidak dipungut biaya.

translated_text:
Article 41

(1) The implementation of handling Women and Children victims of violence as referred to in Article 40 is carried out through integrated services.

(2) Integrated services for Women and Children victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) use the principles of:

a. gender responsive;
b. non-discrimination;
c. equal and respectful relations;
d. maintaining confidentiality;
e. providing a sense of safety and comfort;
f. respecting individual differences;
g. non-judgmental;
h. respecting the choices and decisions of victims; i. being sensitive to the background and conditions of victims and the use of appropriate language understood by victims;
j. fast and simple;
k. empathy;
l. fulfillment of the rights of Women and Children; and m. free of charge.

text:
Pasal 42

Pelayanan penanganan pengaduan korban kekerasan terhadap Perempuan dan Anak dilaksanakan oleh: a. rumah sakit;

b. puskesmas;

c. P2TP2A;

d. Unit Pelayanan Perempuan dan Anak (UPPA); e. Rumah Perlindungan Trauma Center (RPTC); f. Rumah Perlindungan Sosial Anak (RPSA);

g. Women Crisis Centre (WCC)

h. Badan Penasehat Pembinaan dan Pelestarian Perkawinan (BP4);

i. Kepolisian;

j. Kejaksaan;

k. Pengadilan;

l. Lembaga Bantuan Hukum (LBH);

m. Lembaga Perlindungan Anak (LPA);

n. Lembaga Perlindungan Kesejahteraan Sosial; dan o. Rumah Singgah.

translated_text:
Article 42

Complaint handling services for victims of violence against Women and Children are carried out by: a. hospitals;

b. community health centers;

c. P2TP2A;

d. Women and Children Service Units (UPPA); e. Trauma Center Protection Houses (RPTC); f. Child Social Protection Houses (RPSA);

g. Women Crisis Centre (WCC)

h. Marriage Advisory, Guidance and Preservation Board (BP4);

i. Police;

j. Prosecutor's Office;

k. Court;

l. Legal Aid Institute (LBH);

m. Child Protection Institute (LPA);

n. Social Welfare Protection Institute; and o. Shelters.

text:
Pasal 44

(1) Pelayanan kesehatan bagi Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan meliputi aspek:

a. Promotif;
b. Preventif;
c. Kuratif;
d. rehabilitatif.
(2) Pelayanan kesehatan bagi Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan dilakukan secara:
a. Komprehensif;
b. dapat diakses 24 (dua puluh empat) jam;
c. berkualitas; dan
d. sesuai dengan standar pelayanan kesehatan. (3) Pelayanan kesehatan khusus untuk Anak korban kekerasan, harus mendahulukan kepentingan terbaik untuk Anak.
(4) perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan berhak terhadap pelayanan kesehatan, meliputi:
a. pelayanan medis;
b. pelayanan medikolegal; dan
c. konseling psikososial.
(5) Ketentuan lebih lanjut mengenai tata cara pelaksanaan pelayanan kesehatan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (4) diatur dengan Peraturan Daerah.

translated_text:
Article 44

(1) Health services for Women and Children victims of violence include the aspects of:

a. Promotive;
b. Preventive;
c. Curative;
d. rehabilitative.
(2) Health services for Women and Children victims of violence are carried out:
a. Comprehensively;
b. accessible 24 (twenty-four) hours;
c. with quality; and
d. in accordance with health service standards. (3) Special health services for Children victims of violence must prioritize the best interests of the Child.
(4) Women and Children victims of violence are entitled to health services, including:
a. medical services;
b. medicolegal services; and
c. psychosocial counseling.
(5) Further provisions regarding the procedures for implementing health services as referred to in paragraph (4) shall be regulated by Regional Regulation.

text:
Pasal 45

(1) Pelayanan rehabilitasi sosial bagi Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan ditujukan untuk memulihkan dan mengembangkan kemampuan korban yang mengalami disfungsi sosial untuk dapat melaksanakan fungsi sosialnya dalam masyarakat secara wajar.

(2) Pelayanan rehabilitasi sosial sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi:

a. pelayanan konseling;
b. penyediaan rumah aman;
c. bimbingan rohani.
(3) Penyelenggaraan pelayanan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) diselenggarakan oleh:
a. Perangkat Daerah yang mempunyai tugas dan berfungsi di bidang sosial;
b. DPPKBPP-PA;
c. P2TP2A;
d. Women Crisis Centre (WeC);
e. organisasi kemasyarakatan bidang sosial; dan/ atau
f. instansi keagamaan.

translated_text:
Article 45

(1) Social rehabilitation services for Women and Children victims of violence are aimed at restoring and developing the capacity of victims experiencing social dysfunction to be able to carry out their social functions in society properly.

(2) Social rehabilitation services as referred to in paragraph (1) include:

a. counseling services;
b. provision of safe houses;
c. spiritual guidance.
(3) The provision of services as referred to in paragraph (2) is organized by:
a. Regional Apparatus having duties and functions in the social field;
b. DPPKBPP-PA;
c. P2TP2A;
d. Women Crisis Centre (WCC);
e. community organizations in the social field; and/ or
f. religious institutions.

text:
Pasal 46

(1) Pelayanan konseling sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 45 ayat (2) huruf a bertujuan:

a. membantu korban mengenali permasalahannya dan menemukan cara-cara yang efektif untuk mengatasinya sendiri;
b. memberdayakan korban untuk menentukan masa depannya;
c. memberikan dukungan moral bagi korban dalam menghadapi proses yang dijalaninya; dan
d. membuat korban merasa diterima di lingkungan masyarakat.
(2) Pelayanan konseling dilakukan oleh petugas rehabilitasi sosial yang responsif gender, terdiri atas: a. konselor;
b. psikolog; dan
c. psikiater.
(3) Pelayanan konseling dilakukan di tempat yang menjamin rasa aman, nyaman dan kerahasiaan informasi dari korban.
(4) Tahapan pelayanan konseling meliputi:
a. konseling awal;
b. konseling lanjutan;
c. pembahasan kasus (Case conference); dan d. kunjungan ke lokasi (home visit).

translated_text:
Article 46

(1) Counseling services as referred to in Article 45 paragraph (2) letter a aim to:

a. help victims recognize their problems and find effective ways to overcome them themselves;
b. empower victims to determine their future;
c. provide moral support for victims in facing the processes they undergo; and
d. make victims feel accepted in the community environment.
(2) Counseling services are carried out by gender-responsive social rehabilitation officers, consisting of: a. counselors;
b. psychologists; and
c. psychiatrists.
(3) Counseling services are carried out in a place that guarantees a sense of safety, comfort and confidentiality of information from victims.
(4) The stages of counseling services include:
a. initial counseling;
b. follow-up counseling;
c. case conference; and d. home visit.

text:
Pasal 48

(1) Setiap Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan diberikan bimbingan rohani yang ditujukan untuk pemulihan kejiwaan.

(2) Bimbingan rohani sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan berdasarkan prinsip :

a. tidak memaksakan agama atau keyakinan apapun; dan
b. menyerahkan putusan akhir di tangan korban (self determination).
(3) Bimbingan rohani sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) dilakukan oleh petugas bimbingan rohani.
(4) Petugas bimbingan rohani sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (3) terdiri dari:
a. konsultan Badan Penasehatan, Pembinaan dan Pelestarian Perkawinan (BP4);
b. Petugas Kantor Urusan Agama (KUA);
c. Ustad atau Ulama;
d. Pastor;
e. Pendeta; dan
f. pemuka agama lainnya yang memiliki kepekaan gender atau kesadaran gender.

translated_text:
Article 48

(1) Every Woman and Child victim of violence is provided spiritual guidance aimed at psychological recovery.

(2) Spiritual guidance as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out based on the principles:

a. not imposing any religion or belief; and
b. leaving the final decision in the hands of the victim (self determination).
(3) Spiritual guidance as referred to in paragraph (2) is carried out by spiritual guidance officers.
(4) Spiritual guidance officers as referred to in paragraph (3) consist of:
a. consultants of the Advisory, Development and Preservation of Marriage Agency (BP4);
b. Officers of the Religious Affairs Office (KUA);
c. Ustads or Islamic scholars;
d. Priests;
e. Ministers; and
f. other religious leaders who have gender sensitivity or gender awareness.

text:
Pasal 50

(1) Pelayanan penegakan dan bantuan hukum sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 49 ditujukan untuk memberikan pendampingan dan perlindungan terhadap Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan dan saksi dengan pendekatan responsif gender agar korban mendapatkan keadilan dan kepastian hak hukum.

(2) Jenis pelayanan bantuan hukum sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi:

a. bantuan hukum dalam proses pelaporan dan pembuatan BAP;
b. bantuan hukum dalam proses penuntutan di kejaksaan;
c. bantuan hukum dalam proses pemeriksaan di pengadilan;
d. bantuan hukum dalam proses putusan sidang pengadilan sampai adanya keputusan hukum tetap; dan
e. bantuan hukum dalam proses mediasi.
(3) Pemerintah Kabupaten memberikan bantuan hukum kepada Anak dan Perempuan korban kekerasan secara bebas biaya.
(4) Dalam pemberian bantuan hukum sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (3) Pemerintah Kabupaten dapat bekerjasama dengan:
a. Lembaga Bantuan Hukum (LBH);
b. Women Crisis Center (WCC);
c. Advokat; dan / atau
d. pendamping hukum lainnya yang sensitif gender.

translated_text:
Article 50

(1) Law enforcement services and legal assistance as referred to in Article 49 are aimed at providing accompaniment and protection to Women and Children victims of violence and witnesses with a gender-responsive approach so that victims obtain justice and legal certainty of rights.

(2) Types of legal assistance services as referred to in paragraph (1) include:

a. legal assistance in the reporting process and preparation of the official report;
b. legal assistance in the prosecution process at the prosecutor's office;
c. legal assistance in the examination process at the court;
d. legal assistance in the court decision process until there is a final legal decision; and
e. legal assistance in the mediation process.
(3) The Regency Government provides legal assistance to Children and Women victims of violence free of charge.
(4) In providing legal assistance as referred to in paragraph (3), the Regency Government may cooperate with:
a. Legal Aid Institutions (LBH);
b. Women Crisis Center (WCC);
c. Advocates; and/or
d. other legal assistants who are gender sensitive.

text:
Pasal 57

(1) Pemerintah Kabupaten melakukan pembinaan kepada Pemerintah Kecamatan dalam pengembangan Kabupaten Layak Anak.

(2) Pembinaan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi:

a. koordinasi;
b. fasilitasi;
c. bimbingan;
d. supervisi;
e. konsultasi; dan
f. pendidikan dan pelatihan.
(3) Ketentuan mengenai Kabupaten Layak Anak diatur lebih lanjut dengan Peraturan Daerah.

